    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272-a1">

                <pb facs="0362" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg254"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Higgins to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Executive Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sacramento
                                Cal.,</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1893-08-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 18, 1893</hi></date>. (Received
                        August 24.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I am directed by the governor to
                    acknowledge receipt of your telegram of this date in relation to the Chinese
                    disturbances in Fresno and Tulare counties.</p>
                <p>Information from the same source (Chinese consul-general at San Francisco)
                    readied the governor yesterday by telegram.</p>
                <p>While the governor does not anticipate any violence or bloodshed, he at once
                    notified the peace officers of the two counties to take all precautionary
                    measures to prevent any outbreaks against the Chinese that should be
                    attempted.</p>
                <p>He has also requested the proper officers of the two counties to keep him
                    informed in relation to the movements and proceedings in such matter.</p>
                <p>Your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. R. Higgins</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Private Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
